1
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,540
Pick a card.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,540
Okay.

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,710
All right. Now memorize it.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,210
You got it?

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,210
Oh, yes.

6
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:12,300
Okay. Is that your card?

7
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:17,550
Yes.

8
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:17,550
Ha, ha.

9
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,810
Hey, guys.

10
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,810
Hi there.

11
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,560
Guess what. Ben is gonna be in a TV commercial.

12
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,650
What are you talking about?

13
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,650
Well, it's not for sure.

14
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:34,700
But, uh, we met this guy in the park who thought Ben was really cute.

15
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:38,370
You know, which he is. Um, anyhoo, he gave us his card...

16
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:41,870
...and told us to bring him down for this commercial he's auditioning.

17
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:43,790
Whoa.

18
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,620
The guy's like the biggest commercial casting director in town.

19
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,710
Ben takes one lousy walk in the park and gets an audition?

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,010
I mean, way to go, Ben!

21
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,220
Man, I've been in that park a million times. No one's ever offered me an audition.

22
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:04,980
I know, it's crazy. We were just pushing Ben on the swings...

23
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,560
I'm always on the swings.

24
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:10,440
What am I doing wrong?

25
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,780
That.

26
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,040
Okay, gotta go. Wish me luck.

27
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,040
Good luck.

28
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:10,370
Hey, Rach, now that you working at Ralph Lauren, can you get me some shirts?

29
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:13,460
Uh, well, you know what? I don't know if I'd feel comfortable stealing...

30
00:02:13,630 --> 00:02:15,630
...on my very first day.

31
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,800
Unwilling to steal from work.

32
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:20,550
Interesting.

33
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,220
Besides, if anybody is gonna get free stuff, it's me.

34
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:25,760
Okay, guys, way to wish me luck.

35
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,480
Go get them.

36
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,480
Bye.

37
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,690
Okay, let's discuss Rachel's birthday.

38
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,190
I say we throw a surprise party this weekend.

39
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,730
Whoa, whoa. But her birthday's not for another month.

40
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:39,190
Okay, but if we throw her a party on her birthday, then it's not a surprise.

41
00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:44,580
I think that's a great idea. We can have a dinner party and invite her close friends.

42
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,080
Ross. We're having a surprise party for Rachel.

43
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,710
Okay.

44
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,710
Done.

45
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,460
Okay, great. So do you wanna do it together?

46
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,420
I would love to do it together.

47
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,680
They're gonna do it together.

48
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:03,590
Dude, that's my girlfriend.

49
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,470
So I gotta shut it down now?

50
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:10,100
All right, I gotta take off. I'm picking up Ben...

51
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:12,640
...and then we're off to the big audition.

52
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:15,900
It's gonna be weird seeing some actor pretending to be Ben's dad.

53
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,650
Yeah.

54
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,650
Weirder than his two moms making out?

55
00:03:20,990 --> 00:03:23,320
Whoa, whoa. Dad? There's a dad in the commercial?

56
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:26,830
Yeah. The dad and Ben eat soup and pretend to enjoy it.

57
00:03:26,990 --> 00:03:29,790
Well, maybe I'll go with you and see if I can audition as the dad.

58
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:32,410
I mean, who better to play Ben's father than his godfather?

59
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,210
You're not his godfather.

60
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,210
What?

61
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:37,960
Are you kidding?

62
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:41,090
Of course I am.

63
00:03:43,130 --> 00:03:46,470
Okay, let's go, godfather.

64
00:03:43,130 --> 00:03:46,470
All right. Ha, ha.

65
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:55,440
Hey, I'm in. They're gonna let me audition.

66
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,150
Really? That's great.

67
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:00,690
I know, I know. One of the casting ladies has actually seen me in a play.

68
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,690
So I steered clear of her.

69
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:06,450
That kid looks familiar.

70
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:06,450
Oh, yeah.

71
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:08,120
Yeah, he's done tons of commercials.

72
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,540
I've seen him in Sugar Smacks, PlayStation...

73
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,330
...and that one for the phone company.

74
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,000
In fact, he was so good in that one...

75
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,790
...he actually convinced me to switch phone companies.

76
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,590
Chandler was mad.

77
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:23,800
Yeah, well, he's not gonna get this one. All right? Ben is way cuter than that kid.

78
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:25,220
I mean, look at him.

79
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:33,560
That's great.

80
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:36,270
Listen, wouldn't it be great if I got to play Ben's dad?

81
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,940
Joey, you look nothing like Ben.

82
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,650
I look more like him than you do.

83
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:47,320
Well, I really don't know you well enough for you to do that.

84
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:56,370
So it's down to these two. Nancy, I know you like this one...

85
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,080
...and I think I agree. Rachel, what do you think?

86
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:01,420
Well, um, that one is pretty...

87
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:05,510
...but I just love this fabric. Sorry.

88
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,390
Oh, don't be. That's part of your job here, to give your opinions.

89
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:11,850
And then I take credit for them. I'm kidding. Ha, ha.

90
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:15,100
She is kidding. But don't ever disagree with her again.

91
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:17,440
Okay, now I'm kidding.

92
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:17,440
Oh, ha, ha.

93
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,690
Oh, what a fun office.

94
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:24,230
I don't know which one. But I do know I need a cigarette.

95
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:26,400
So, what do you say we take a break, go outside...

96
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:28,240
...and figure this out when we come back.

97
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:32,700
Rachel?

98
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:32,700
Yeah.

99
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:33,870
You smoke?

100
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:33,870
No.

101
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:37,910
My dad's a doctor. And he would always tell me just horror stories...

102
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:44,090
About ghosts and goblins...

103
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:49,130
...who totally supported the princess' right to smoke.

104
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:56,770
And then they came back from smoking...

105
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:59,310
...and they'd made all of the decisions without me.

106
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,150
That doesn't seem fair.

107
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,150
I know.

108
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:04,980
It's like I'm being punished for not having this disgusting, poisonous habit.

109
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:06,990
Yeah, it is the best.

110
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:10,200
I mean, what if this keeps happening?

111
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,700
They'll be outside smoking, making all the decisions...

112
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:17,250
...and I'll just be up in my office breathing in my stupid clean air.

113
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:19,960
You know? And when Kim wants to promote one of us...

114
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:23,540
...who do you think she's gonna pick? Me or Smokey Smokerson?

115
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,550
Rachel, you can go down there, you don't have to smoke.

116
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:28,970
Just say you wanna get some fresh air.

117
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,010
Yeah, I could do that.

118
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:34,760
Yeah, or you could just do the easy thing and smoke.

119
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,430
Hey. Do you wanna go get coffee?

120
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,430
Hey.

121
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,480
Oh, I would love to.

122
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,480
Oh, good.

123
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,900
I'm gonna go too, babe.

124
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,900
Oh, good.

125
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,270
Yay.

126
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,270
Yay.

127
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,480
Oh, I changed my mind.

128
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,160
Okay, let's talk about the party. I have so many ideas.

129
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,780
Ooh, me too.

130
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,780
Oh!

131
00:06:56,330 --> 00:06:58,750
Yeah!

132
00:06:56,330 --> 00:06:58,750
Oh, look at that.

133
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:02,620
All right. This is a little sketch of the cake.

134
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:02,620
Uh-huh. Wow.

135
00:07:02,790 --> 00:07:05,340
See? Um, some sample menus.

136
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:08,460
Um, you know, I thought we'd start with a Tuscan-style finger food.

137
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:12,930
Okay. And for music, here's an alphabetized list of all of my CDs.

138
00:07:13,090 --> 00:07:16,300
I've highlighted the ones that'll go really good with the food.

139
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:19,390
What happened to the dinner party?

140
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:19,390
We're not doing that.

141
00:07:19,770 --> 00:07:22,270
Okay? So...

142
00:07:19,770 --> 00:07:22,270
Wow. All right.

143
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:26,060
Looks like you took care of everything. Thanks a lot, cohost.

144
00:07:26,650 --> 00:07:28,360
Wait. I didn't take care of everything.

145
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:30,190
There's plenty of things for you to do.

146
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,070
Uh-huh? Like what?

147
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,570
Cups.

148
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,080
Cups. You're giving me cups?

149
00:07:37,950 --> 00:07:39,540
And ice.

150
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:43,420
Cups and ice? Oh, I get to be in charge of cups and ice?

151
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:45,170
All right.

152
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:49,000
Fine. Okay, I will be in charge of cups and ice.

153
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,510
Wait, I can get ice at the restaurant...

154
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,510
I got it.

155
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,550
Hi.

156
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,550
Hey.

157
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:59,140
How did the audition go?

158
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:59,140
Not so good.

159
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:02,730
Wait a minute. Are you doing Joey's:

160
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:06,940
"The audition didn't go so well. Yeah, it did!"

161
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:09,730
Yeah, I am!

162
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:15,110
Yeah, Ben got a second audition.

163
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:15,110
Oh, great.

164
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:20,120
Yeah, I had to teach Ross my bit because I actually didn't get a callback.

165
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:23,210
You got a callback too, didn't you?

166
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:27,540
Yeah, I did!

167
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:34,840
Hey, Rachel. What are you doing out here?

168
00:08:35,010 --> 00:08:39,350
You know, it got kind of lonely up there, so I just thought I would come out here...

169
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:41,970
...and get some fresh air.

170
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:44,100
We were talking about the fall collection.

171
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,480
Oh, great.

172
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,480
So anyway, we really...

173
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,980
I'm sorry. We're smoking all over you.

174
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,980
That's okay.

175
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:51,780
No, no, no. We'll move. You stay there.

176
00:08:52,690 --> 00:08:55,400
I sent the designs to Ralph. He was excited about it.

177
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:58,320
That's great. You are the best.

178
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,660
Excuse me. Can I bum one of those?

179
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:03,250
Actually, this one's...

180
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,630
Okay, okay, okay. What's so funny over here?

181
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:10,840
I thought you didn't smoke.

182
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:15,840
You know, I thought you guys meant marijuana cigarettes.

183
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,930
You know what I mean? Like, doobies?

184
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:24,220
Actually, I thought to myself, "Those guys are crazy."

185
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,890
But no, actually, I smoke the regular ones all the time.

186
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:28,940
We get high.

187
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:33,320
Me too.

188
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:36,650
I'm kidding.

189
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:36,650
Oh!

190
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:38,700
Me too.

191
00:09:41,410 --> 00:09:44,950
Oh, God. This is so nerve-racking. How do you do this?

192
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:48,120
Well, fortunately, I don't get many callbacks so...

193
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:51,710
Is it a good sign that they asked us to hang around after?

194
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,500
Who knows?

195
00:09:55,210 --> 00:10:01,220
Okay. We have narrowed it down to Raymond, Ben, Kyle and Joey.

196
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:02,970
The rest of you, thank you very much.

197
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,520
Yes! I knew it!

198
00:10:05,890 --> 00:10:08,390
Ah. Bye-bye.

199
00:10:09,350 --> 00:10:11,440
So long.

200
00:10:12,110 --> 00:10:13,400
Later.

201
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:17,820
This is great. I might actually get to play Ben's dad.

202
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:20,240
Actually, that can't happen.

203
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:22,410
Because you all have such different looks...

204
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:25,660
...we're putting you with Raymond and Kyle with Ben.

205
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:28,580
So it'll either be you two or you two.

206
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,790
Oh, man.

207
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:35,500
This is gonna be kind of weird.

208
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:35,500
Yeah, it is.

209
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,720
Yeah. It's gonna be weird.

210
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:44,140
No. We're like best friends. That's why it's weird.

211
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,640
Oh, oh.

212
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:48,350
I thought we were just talking.

213
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:56,230
Hey.

214
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:56,230
Hey.

215
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:59,820
Is it okay if I leave this stuff here till Rachel's birthday party?

216
00:10:59,990 --> 00:11:03,070
Uh, sure. What's in them?

217
00:10:59,990 --> 00:11:03,070
Um, cups.

218
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:07,080
Oh, good, because we got Rachel 800 gallons of water.

219
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:10,210
Seriously, that's a lot of cups.

220
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:12,290
Yeah, well, I'm in charge of cups and ice.

221
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:16,380
And Monica's gonna rue the day that she put me in charge of cups and ice.

222
00:11:18,170 --> 00:11:21,930
You know, I rued the day once. Didn't get a whole lot else done.

223
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,220
Okay, time to bring up the rest of the cups.

224
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,730
Hey, Joey.

225
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,730
Hey, Pheebs.

226
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:33,850
Hey.

227
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:33,850
Ross, good, I'm glad you're here.

228
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:37,440
I want to talk to you about something.

229
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:37,440
Oh. What's up?

230
00:11:37,610 --> 00:11:40,990
Well, I've been thinking about this whole commercial thing.

231
00:11:41,150 --> 00:11:42,360
You know me against Ben.

232
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:47,280
The two of us competing. Well, that can't lead to anything good.

233
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:50,080
I think I'm just gonna step aside.

234
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:52,960
I'm gonna tell them that I won't audition.

235
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,210
Wow. Uh...

236
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:58,460
Joey, that's great. Thanks, man.

237
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:04,680
That's it?

238
00:12:05,970 --> 00:12:09,220
You're gonna let me do this? This is my career we're talking about here.

239
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:10,520
But you just...

240
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,350
I just said that so you wouldn't let Ben do it.

241
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:16,810
Look, Ross, if anyone should step aside, it should be Ben.

242
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,610
What?

243
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,610
Chandler, tell him.

244
00:12:21,650 --> 00:12:24,490
Well, let me get the door first.

245
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:27,870
Oh, hi, no one.

246
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,870
Why should Ben step aside?

247
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:36,460
It was his audition in the first place. You just tagged along.

248
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,290
You're like the tag-along dad.

249
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:41,170
At least I care about his feelings.

250
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:42,710
What?

251
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,720
Do you know how hard this is gonna be on him when he doesn't get it?

252
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:48,140
And why wouldn't he get it?

253
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,180
Oh, come on.

254
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:53,180
Have you seen what my kid can do? Huh?

255
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:56,640
I mean, he dials phones, he eats tortilla chips.

256
00:12:56,810 --> 00:13:00,060
He plays soccer with the cartoon tiger.

257
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:04,280
Are you saying your kid eats soup better than my kid?

258
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:07,240
You just give him a spoon, baby.

259
00:13:07,410 --> 00:13:09,740
Oh, yeah? I guess we'll see.

260
00:13:07,410 --> 00:13:09,740
Yeah.

261
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:11,990
Because this commercial belongs to me and Mitch.

262
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:15,910
Your kid's name is Raymond.

263
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:15,910
Yeah? So is yours.

264
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:23,170
How did work go?

265
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:23,170
Oh, it was great. It was great.

266
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:26,380
I went down there just like you said. And we talked business.

267
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:28,090
And Kim totally took my opinions.

268
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:29,930
You stink.

269
00:13:31,850 --> 00:13:34,180
Thanks.

270
00:13:31,850 --> 00:13:34,180
No, I'm serious.

271
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:36,680
That's because I went down there and they were smoking.

272
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:39,440
This is actually the smell of success.

273
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,400
But there's something different, though.

274
00:13:42,570 --> 00:13:44,280
Oh, my God. You smoked.

275
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:47,400
I did not.

276
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:47,400
Yes, you did.

277
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:50,200
You look happy and sick. You smoked.

278
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:54,450
All right, fine. But I had to. I had to do it for my career.

279
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,410
I wish I had to smoke for my career.

280
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:00,420
That's so gross.

281
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,670
Well, no, it's not that bad, you know?

282
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:07,720
I mean, yeah, my tongue feels a little fuzzy and my fingers sort of smell.

283
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,340
I actually feel like I could throw up.

284
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:15,970
But you gotta push past this, okay? Because it's about to get so good.

285
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,180
Chandler.

286
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:21,730
You smell so smoky, I gotta get up.

287
00:14:22,310 --> 00:14:23,730
I'm not kidding.

288
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,110
I think you smell great.

289
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:34,410
So we're decided. No on plaid, yes on pink.

290
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:36,080
Absolutely.

291
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:38,790
I'm so onboard.

292
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,130
Rachel, didn't you just light that?

293
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,130
Yeah.

294
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:44,420
But you know what?

295
00:14:44,590 --> 00:14:48,380
I'm just really, really trying to cut back, you know.

296
00:14:48,550 --> 00:14:50,170
Good luck, Rach.

297
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:54,180
I've actually been thinking about quitting.

298
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:56,810
Oh, well, sure. Every Sunday night, I tell myself I'm quitting.

299
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,020
Every Monday morning, it's like:

300
00:14:59,350 --> 00:15:00,520
Tell me about it.

301
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:03,350
Well, let's quit. We'll just quit. Let's all quit.

302
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:04,940
It does sound appealing.

303
00:15:05,110 --> 00:15:07,860
I never could do it.

304
00:15:05,110 --> 00:15:07,860
But you could. You can. Absolutely.

305
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:11,070
We can help each other out. We could get those patches.

306
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,620
We could be like the Patch Sisters.

307
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:17,330
You know, we really should quit. Okay, let's quit.

308
00:15:17,490 --> 00:15:19,620
Yes. Great. Give me those cigs. Come on.

309
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:22,000
Give it. Give it. Out. Done. Quit. Whoo!

310
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,750
My late husband gave me that lighter.

311
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,750
Ha, ha.

312
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,340
I'm not kidding.

313
00:15:31,090 --> 00:15:32,590
Okay, then. Okay.

314
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:44,060
Mm, soup.

315
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,610
Joey, Ross is gonna be here any second.

316
00:15:46,770 --> 00:15:49,150
Would you mind watching Ben while I use the ladies' room?

317
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,530
Yeah, no problem.

318
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,530
Thanks.

319
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:54,110
Mm.

320
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:02,830
Hi, Ben.

321
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:07,460
So you want to be an actor, huh? Well, I gotta tell you, it's no picnic.

322
00:16:07,630 --> 00:16:10,960
There's tons of rejection. No stability.

323
00:16:11,130 --> 00:16:14,930
I mean, one day, you're Dr. Drake Ramoray.

324
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:18,810
The next day, you're eating ketchup right out of the bottle.

325
00:16:21,350 --> 00:16:22,930
Joey.

326
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,980
Ross.

327
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:28,730
Ben.

328
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,030
I mean, Ben. Ben.

329
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,900
Okay, Raymond, Joey, you're up.

330
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,950
Hi.

331
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,950
Okay.

332
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:43,500
All right, well, let's try one. Whenever you guys are ready.

333
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,960
Uh-oh.

334
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,960
Is there a problem?

335
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:50,920
Well, this is noodle soup. And I've been working with tomato.

336
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:53,630
But that's okay. No problem. No problem.

337
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:56,010
Mm, noodle soup.

338
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:59,550
You know, that's fine. But the line is, "Mm, soup."

339
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,680
Oh. What'd I say?

340
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,680
Mm, noodle soup.

341
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:06,060
How's that different?

342
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,690
Oh. Right. Yeah.

343
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:15,070
All right. Let's try one.

344
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,780
Mm, noodle soup.

345
00:17:24,830 --> 00:17:27,080
Okay. Let's do it again.

346
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:28,580
Okay.

347
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:33,460
Mm, soup.

348
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:35,670
I mean, noodle soup. I mean, soup.

349
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:36,840
Come on!

350
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,010
You know what? We need to move on.

351
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,180
Oh, no, I could do it one more time.

352
00:17:44,350 --> 00:17:45,600
See, look.

353
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:47,940
Mm, noodle soup.

354
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,400
Damn it.

355
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,870
Hey. Hey.

356
00:18:01,030 --> 00:18:02,950
Uh-oh. Busted.

357
00:18:03,910 --> 00:18:06,330
Come on, you guys. What are you doing?

358
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,250
I thought we were the Patch Sisters.

359
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,040
Yeah, that didn't work out.

360
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:14,500
Rachel, we tried to quit. But it was too hard.

361
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:18,050
Well, if you started smoking again, you could have at least told me.

362
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:20,890
Come on, give me one of those. What are we talking about?

363
00:18:21,050 --> 00:18:22,680
No, you're doing great. Don't give up.

364
00:18:22,850 --> 00:18:25,640
That's why we didn't tell you, and we are not gonna drag you down.

365
00:18:25,810 --> 00:18:28,060
Oh, wait. No, no. Drag me down. Drag me down.

366
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:31,020
Forget it, Rachel. We're both so proud of how well you're doing.

367
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:34,480
I'm not gonna let you blow it. In fact, if I catch you, you're fired.

368
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:38,570
So go on, get out of here. Go on. I don't want you breathing this stuff. Go on.

369
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:41,450
So okay. So you'll come with me on the Paris trip?

370
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:43,410
Oh, man.

371
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:51,750
Hey, check it out. Cup hat, cup banner...

372
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:55,840
...cup chandelier and the thing that started it all. The cup.

373
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,510
Great job with the cups, Pheebs.

374
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,510
Ha, ha.

375
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:02,300
Why don't you just go out with her?

376
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:06,100
Did you notice the ice? Look.

377
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:10,730
We have it all. We have crushed, cubed and dry. Watch.

378
00:19:10,890 --> 00:19:12,520
Ah.

379
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:15,020
Mystical.

380
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:23,490
No one's eating my Tuscan finger food. They're filling up on Phoebe's snow cones.

381
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:25,280
There are snow cones?

382
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:27,160
Snow cones. Yuck.

383
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,950
Go, go.

384
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,950
Thank you. Thank you.

385
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:36,290
Look, look.

386
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:36,290
Surprise.

387
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:40,130
What? My birthday is not for another month.

388
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:42,510
That's the surprise.

389
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:47,930
Oh, my God, you guys. This is so great. It's so unexpected.

390
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:51,310
I mean, Chandler's birthday's even before mine.

391
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,520
Surprise.

392
00:19:59,190 --> 00:20:03,450
Wow. This is so great. Look at all these...

393
00:20:03,610 --> 00:20:06,660
...cups. This is so weird.

394
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:09,080
I was in charge of cups.

395
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,330
Oh, okay. Not so weird.

396
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,460
Hey.

397
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,460
Hey.

398
00:20:16,630 --> 00:20:20,340
Listen, man. I'm sorry the audition didn't go well.

399
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:22,510
Yeah, right.

400
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:25,470
No, really. I am, Joey. I feel bad.

401
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:29,180
Well, look, Ross. You don't have to, okay?

402
00:20:29,350 --> 00:20:31,060
It's not your fault I suck.

403
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:35,100
What kind of an actor can't even say, "Mm, noodle soup"?

404
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:44,360
Hey, you know what? Maybe you didn't mess up your audition because you suck.

405
00:20:44,530 --> 00:20:49,660
Maybe you messed up because you care more about your godson.

406
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,540
What do you mean?

407
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,540
I think, subconsciously...

408
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:55,290
Whoa, you lost me.

409
00:20:59,670 --> 00:21:03,630
I think, on some level, you sabotaged...

410
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:07,840
...your own audition so Ben would get the part.

411
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:13,180
Well, your way sounds a lot better than mine.

412
00:21:13,890 --> 00:21:15,480
Yeah.

413
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,310
Yeah. It's not that I'm a bad actor.

414
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,310
No.

415
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:22,570
No, it's just that, uh, I care so damn much about little Ben...

416
00:21:22,730 --> 00:21:26,110
...that, uh, it was more important for me to see him succeed.

417
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,860
There you go. Thank you.

418
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,860
Thank you.

419
00:21:29,030 --> 00:21:30,910
So did he get it?

420
00:21:29,030 --> 00:21:30,910
No.

421
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,450
Ah, what are you gonna do?

422
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:42,250
Oh, hi. Excuse me. Is Rachel Green here? I'm supposed to meet her for lunch.

423
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:45,420
Oh, she doesn't come down anymore. You can find her up on 10.

424
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:47,010
Okay, great.

425
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:50,140
So we talked about the presentation at lunch.

426
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:53,180
He wondered if one person would be enough for me to take on the trip.

427
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:55,810
And I said, "Yeah, absolutely."

428
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:02,940
I'll catch you guys later.

